===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰed-}}
From {{der|en|fro|-}} via {{der|en|enm|-}} and {{der|en|frm|entreprise}}, feminine past participle of {{m|fro|entreprendre||to undertake}}, from {{m|frm|entre||in between}} + {{m|fro|prendre||to take}}, from Latin {{m|la|inter}} + {{m|la|prehendō}}, see {{m|en|prehensile}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛntəˌpɹaɪz/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛntɚˌpɹaɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-enterprise.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|en|ter|prise}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|company}} A [[company]], business, organization, or other purposeful [[endeavor]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:enterprise}}
#: ''The government sponsored '''enterprises''' (GSEs) are a group of financial services corporations which have been created by the United States Congress.''
#: ''A micro-'''enterprise''' is defined as a company or business having 5 or fewer employees and a low seed capital.''
# {{senseid|en|undertaking}} An [[undertaking]], [[venture]], or [[project]], especially a daring and [[courageous]] one.
#: ''Biosphere 2 was a scientific '''enterprise''' aimed at the exploration of the complex web of interactions within life systems.''
# {{senseid|en|willingness}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[willingness]] to undertake new or risky projects; energy and initiative.
#: ''He has shown great '''enterprise''' throughout his early career.''
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1954|author=w:Philip Larkin|title=Continuing to Live
|passage=This loss of interest, hair, and '''enterprise''' — / Ah, if the game were poker, yes, / You might discard them, draw a full house! / But it's chess.}}
# {{senseid|en|participation}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} Active participation in projects. {{rfex|en}}

