===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To undertake an enterprise, or something hazardous or difficult.
#* {{RQ:Pope Horace|passage=Charles Mordaunt Earl of Peterborow{{...}}, with only 280 horse and 950 foot , '''enterprised''' and accomplished the Conquest of Valentia }}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[undertake]]; to begin and attempt to perform; to venture upon.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1670|author=w:John Dryden|title=w:The Conquest of Granada
|passage=The business must be '''enterprised''' this night.}}
#* '''c. 1680''', {{w|Thomas Otway}}, letter to {{w|Elizabeth Barry}}
#*: What would I not renounce or '''enterprise''' for you!
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To treat with [[hospitality]]; to [[entertain]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|canto=II|book=II|stanza=14|passage=Him at the threshold met, and well did '''enterprize'''.}}

